      "role": "user",
      "content": "I see. So it sounds like the diversity itself is the driver of the volatility. If we were comparing this to a more homogeneous market in Eastern Europe or parts of East Asia, wouldn't the absence of these ethnic friction points make those regions fundamentally more \"stable\" for long-term capital? It seems like these multi-ethnic African markets have a built-in instability that you just don't see in more unified nations.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
